// Rule: [T1027.013] Valleyrat - Qnwallpaper Peloader
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1027.013
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceFileEvents
// Purpose: Exact file-metadata hunt for the AES encrypted backdoor artifact staged by the source-observed QNWallpaper delivery chain. A match is not proof of memory loading, persistence...
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceFileEvents for qnwallpaper peloader using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceFileEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: A match is not proof of payload execution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// ValleyRAT QNWallpaper PeLoader artifact
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Telemetry prerequisite: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / DeviceFileEvents
// Scope: exact source-observed campaign artifact. A match is not proof of payload execution.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FileName == "PeLoader"
| where FolderPath startswith @"C:\\Program Files\\QNWallpaper\\5.4.0.1662\\"
| where MD5 =~ "48826d5ca845979d2e6ebd66dc1aae90"
| project Timestamp,
          DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType,
          FileName, FolderPath, FileSize,
          MD5, SHA1, SHA256,
          FileOriginUrl, FileOriginReferrerUrl, FileOriginIP,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessMD5,
          InitiatingProcessSHA1, InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
